+# Kawun residual C — locked ESLint rule gap, Founder authorization required
+
+**Seat:** c1a00002 (Executive liaison)
+**Date:** 2026-10-16
+**Issue:** Kawun #155 review blocker; also cited as the #195 landing blocker.
+**Verdict:** REAL gap. Fix requires modifying a **Founder-locked** ESLint rule. Viche must not do this without an explicit direct Founder instruction. Authorization requested.
+
+## 1. The gap (reproduced)
+
+`source/kawunapp/tools/eslint-plugin-kawun/rules/directory-imports.js` handles only
+`ImportDeclaration` (static `import ... from '...'`). It has **no** handler for
+`ImportExpression` (dynamic `import('...')`). Therefore a cross-directory deep
+import written as `await import('.../internal/file.ts')` draws **no report** and
+all gates stay green.
+
+This matters beyond style: Kawun's capability model uses *reachability* for module
+visibility (see #155), so a deep dynamic import can reach an internal module (and
+its authority) that the index-only rule is supposed to keep unreachable.
+
+Reproduction (2026-10-16, on `origin/main` @ `a30afa45`): adding an
+`ImportExpression` handler to the rule and running `npm run lint` surfaces
+**8 real violations** that the current rule misses:
+
+| File | Specifier |
+|---|---|
+| `src/backend/features/pickleball/service/tests/defaults.test.tsx:20` | `../../../../../../tests/pwa/a11y/harness.ts` |
+| `src/backend/features/pickleball/service/tests/wiring.test.tsx:16` | `../../../../../../tests/pwa/a11y/harness.ts` |
+| `src/modules/views/admin/tests/defaults.test.tsx:20` | `../../../../../tests/pwa/a11y/harness.ts` |
+| `src/modules/views/admin/tests/defaultsSeam.test.tsx:23` | `../../../../../tests/pwa/a11y/harness.ts` |
+| `tests/pwa/entry/entryBrowser.ts:27` | `../../../src/main.tsx` |
+| `tests/pwa/entry/open.test.ts:21` | `../a11y/harness.ts` |
+| `tests/pwa/entry/optionality.test.ts:22` | `../a11y/harness.ts` |
+| `tests/pwa/entry/wiring.test.ts:21` | `../a11y/harness.ts` |
+
+The rule change was applied, measured, and **reverted**; no locked file is modified
+in the tree.
+
+## 2. Why Viche cannot self-execute this
+
+Two Founder-owned records forbid it:
+
+- `source/kawunapp/docs/intent-record/engineering.md`, id `1327469051846307`
+  (title "ESLint and policy rules are locked", `source: @ottojung`):
+  *"Agents and ordinary repository work must not modify, weaken, disable, remove,
+  relax, replace, or bypass them. Changing this policy requires a new direct
+  trusted user instruction explicitly authorizing the policy change."*
+- `source/kawunapp/AGENTS.md`: *"Changing locked policy requires an explicit
+  direct user-authorized intent change."*
+
+`rules/directory-imports.js` is inside the locked surface
+(`policy/locked-surface.mjs`, `pluginDirectory = 'tools/eslint-plugin-kawun'`),
+so the `check-locked` hash gate must be re-pinned after any change.
+
+## 3. Prepared patch (unapplied; for immediate use on authorization)
+
+Rule (`rules/directory-imports.js`) — factor the check and add the dynamic case:
+
+```js
+'use strict';
+
+const path = require('node:path');
+const { INDEX_BASENAMES, resolveImportTarget } = require('../lib');
+
+module.exports = {
+  meta: {
+    type: 'suggestion',
+    docs: {
+      description: 'Import across directories only through their index.',
+    },
+    schema: [],
+    messages: {
+      deep: 'Import "{{specifier}}" through the directory index, not an'
+        + ' internal file.',
+    },
+  },
+  create(context) {
+    const current = path.dirname(context.filename);
+
+    function reportDeep(node, specifier) {
+      const target = resolveImportTarget(context.filename, specifier);
+      if (!target) return;
+      if (path.dirname(target) === current) return;
+      if (INDEX_BASENAMES.includes(path.basename(target))) return;
+      context.report({ node, messageId: 'deep', data: { specifier } });
+    }
+
+    return {
+      ImportDeclaration(node) {
+        reportDeep(node, node.source.value);
+      },
+      ImportExpression(node) {
+        const { source } = node;
+        if (source.type !== 'Literal') return;
+        if (typeof source.value !== 'string') return;
+        reportDeep(node, source.value);
+      },
+    };
+  },
+};
+```
+
+Test additions (`tests/directory-imports.test.js`), proven green:
+valid `import('../lib')`, `import('./max-line-length')`, `import(name)`;
+invalid `import('../lib/limits.js')`.
+
+Non-locked companion edits (7 of the 8 sites are mechanical — point them at the
+directory index `tests/pwa/a11y/index.ts`, which already re-exports `hooks`):
+
+- the 4 `src/**/tests/*.tsx` and the 3 `tests/pwa/entry/*.test.ts` imports above.
+
+The 8th site needs a decision: `tests/pwa/entry/entryBrowser.ts` deliberately
+**executes** the composition root `src/main.tsx` (the app entry that calls
+`createRoot` and arms the service-worker listener); there is no index that
+re-exports it, and importing `src/index.ts` would not run the bootstrap. Options:
+(a) a single, justified `eslint-disable-next-line` on that one line; or
+(b) extend the rule to treat `main.*` as an allowed entry surface alongside
+`index.*`. Recommendation: (a) — narrowest, auditable, no rule semantics change.
+
+## 4. Requested authorization (exact wording)
+
+> Founder: authorize the locked-policy change to Kawun's `kawun/directory-imports`
+> ESLint rule (intent record `1327469051846307`) adding `ImportExpression`
+> coverage so dynamic `import()` cannot bypass the index-only import constraint,
+> together with the mechanical companion edits to the 7 listed test imports and
+> the single justified disable at `tests/pwa/entry/entryBrowser.ts`.
+
+If the Founder declines, residual C is recorded as an accepted limitation and
+#155/#195 are closed/annotated on that basis.
+
+## 5. #195 landing assessment (measured 2026-10-16)
+
+`origin/main` and `origin/release/along-long-namespace` diverged at `d300b5e3`:
+**128** commits on the release line that main lacks, **178** on main that the
+release line lacks; full diff **622 files, +13785 / −14580**.
+
+A trial merge (local, `--no-commit`, then aborted; no ref moved) produced **35
+conflicted files**, including `package.json`, `policy/locked-policy.json`, several
+barrel `index.ts` files, and a batch of add/add test files under
+`tests/secret-url/`.
+
+Conclusion: landing the release line is a deliberate, reviewed integration
+effort — not a bounded single-agent action — and `main` is the production deploy
+branch (`kawunapp-deploy.yml`). Viche should not perform a unilateral wholesale
+merge. Recommended: a dedicated integration front with conflict-resolution,
+full-gate verification at the merged head, and independent review; or a decision
+that main has superseded the release line and #195 is closed as such.
+
+## 6. Recommendation
+
+Escalate once, concisely, with the prepared patch ready (done 2026-10-16 via Town
+Hall #297). Do not modify the locked rule without the instruction above. Do not
+perform a unilateral wholesale merge of `release/along-long-namespace` into `main`.
